<mxfile host="www.iodraw.com" agent="Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/155.0.0.0 Safari/537.36" version="24.7.17" pages="2">
  <diagram id="wdxr-ksmw0wqOJfV0Th9" name="Page-2">
    <mxGraphModel dx="778" dy="413" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="EH43Kf83GVdlbr7WDXlS-1" value="Agam RTK Base test as standalone device&amp;nbsp;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=18;fontStyle=4" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="230" y="45" width="370" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="EH43Kf83GVdlbr7WDXlS-2" value="2 Agam RTK Base was used, one as RTK base and the other as RTK Rover.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Aim of the test&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;To use 2 Agam RTK Bases, one as Base and other as Rover to achieve RTK- Fix as GNSS fix type.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use the Base RTK as independent device powered by a battery, and transmitting the RTCM correction data through a wireless telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Using no other software than ublox u-center2 to record the data.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="80" width="790" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="LBVvRoIkureotuKAEjZE-1" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Test setup&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The test setup and connections are shown&amp;nbsp; as diagram on the next page.&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="260" width="410" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="LBVvRoIkureotuKAEjZE-2" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Configurations of GNSS modules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;The Base RTK is powered by a battery, and not connected to any PC at all times. The configuration on the RTK Base module for survey-in and&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;RTCM outputs was done before&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;by connecting it to u-center2 software through USB. And the RTK Rover module is connected to the PC through&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;USB port and to the u-center2 software, telemetry being received on UART1 port through wireless telemetry.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Since the telemetry used works on the baud rate 57600, therefore the baud rate for UART1 port of both the modules used in Base and Rover&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;was changed to 57600 through u-center2 software.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;All the configurtions done on these 2 GNSS modules are shown in the setup diagram itself.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="350" width="790" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="LBVvRoIkureotuKAEjZE-3" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Observations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;When survey-in process on Base completes, it starts transmitting the RTCM correction through telemetry. After few seconds, the Rover goes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;into RTK-fix mode and the accuracy in position seem to be drastically improved. Also the blue LED on rover glows solid on acheiving RTK-fix&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;(image below). With&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;RTK-float, the Blue LED Blinks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;In the table view of u-center2, all the parameters can be selected to be recorded which includes longitude, latitude, altitude, time, number of&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;satellites etc. The recorded data was exported as csv, which might look something like:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="555" width="770" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="LBVvRoIkureotuKAEjZE-4" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="39.16" y="750" width="751.67" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
